# This is an EXUDYN example
#
# Details:  Flexible body with the floating frame of reference formulation: Notebook
#           `python/Notebooks/tutorialFFRF.ipynb`. A flexible pendulum with the floating frame of reference
#           formulation (FFRF): Netgen meshes it and NGsolve computes the finite element matrices, the body is
#           reduced to Hurty-Craig-Bampton modes, and it hangs on a revolute joint. It needs the package ngsolve
#           (`pip install ngsolve`). The outputs below each cell are those of the last run.
#
